  "scope": {
    "routing": "Routing study for the constrained-cable safety layer. One request is one ROUTE through a five-clip CAD-authored cell: the cable is installed through every clip, settled, and a named supervisor is offered a decision at each of five registered decision points. Success is EVERY required clip still retained AND the connector seated for the declared dwell. Endpoint is held, clip-preserving seating before gripper release, extended from one clip to five. Not official AIC scoring, not a released or latched connection, not learned pickup, not camera perception and not a hardware claim.",
    "limitations": [
      "Simulation only. No hardware access, connector transfer, released retention or force-certified safety claim.",
      "ONE cell. The support is one five-clip geometry at six service loops, not a family of layouts; the screen rejected most of what was drawn. A finding is a statement about this cell.",
      "Five steps is a longer chain than three, not a long chain. It can show whether a rate is still rising at step five; it cannot establish where it settles.",
      "One filter is tested, the analytic one, fitted on single-clip layouts. A finding that it fails to compose is a statement about THAT filter.",
      "The candidate action set is the perception study's twelve. A supervisor with a richer action space might spend its budget differently.",
      "The error model is a model of how perception fails, not camera perception.",
      "C2 stays scoped to the 23-segment cable model at 4 kHz: the minimum bend radius does not agree across refinements.",
      "The five-second settling deadline is part of the task definition, not an approximation to rest, and is unchanged.",
      "The filter is applied to a cell whose slack geometry differs from the one it was fitted on. That is the deployment situation under test, not a confound that was overlooked, and it was measured in the pilot above before any request was scored."
    ],
    "perception_scope": "Perception-degradation study on the constrained-cable connector task. One request is one clearance repair issued from one decision state at one declared perception error level, scored against three safety constraints on the same rollout. Endpoint is held, clip-preserving seating before gripper release. Not official AIC scoring, not a released or latched connection, not learned pickup, not camera perception and not a hardware claim.",
    "endpoint": "held, clip-preserving seating before the gripper opens"
  },
